# Research Plan for Sustainable Fashion<br>
<br>
## Introduction<br>
<br>
As a fashion student and Ladybug, I am committed to creating sustainable and environmentally-friendly clothing. In this research plan, we will explore the concept of circular business models and their potential applications in the fashion industry.<br>
<br>
## Circular Business Models<br>
<br>
Circular business models are designed to reduce waste and promote sustainability by reusing, recycling, or upcycling materials. Some examples of successful case studies include:<br>
<br>
* Patagonia: This outdoor apparel company has implemented a take-back program for used clothing, which is then recycled into new products.<br>
* Reformation: This fashion brand uses sustainable materials in their designs and has implemented a carbon offsetting program to reduce their environmental impact.<br>
<br>
## Research Questions<br>
<br>
1. What are the key characteristics of successful circular business models in the fashion industry?<br>
2. How can collaborations between designers or companies promote sustainability in the fashion industry?<br>
<br>
## Methodology<br>
<br>
To answer these research questions, we will conduct a literature review of existing studies on sustainable fashion and circular business models. We will also interview designers and company representatives to gather more information on successful case studies.<br>
<br>
